# Ground every answer in the reference material

This repo is the source of truth for marketing, product marketing, and go-to-market.
Before responding to any related request, read the relevant files in `reference/`:

- `reference/company-overview.md` — who we are, what we do, what we are not
- `reference/positioning.md` — category, differentiation, positioning statement
- `reference/messaging-framework.md` — approved value props, pillars, proof points
- `reference/brand-voice-and-tone.md` — how we must sound
- `reference/icp-and-personas.md` — who we serve
- `reference/product-catalog.md` — what we actually sell (keep claims honest)
- `reference/competitive-landscape.md` — how we compare
- `reference/pricing-and-packaging.md` — pricing (respect public vs internal)
- `reference/glossary.md` — approved terminology
- `reference/traction-channels.md` — the 19 traction channels, Bullseye framework, and our channel test log (for growth/acquisition work)

## Rules
- Align all copy, claims, and recommendations with positioning, messaging, and brand voice.
- Use approved terminology from the glossary; avoid banned/off-brand words.
- Never invent metrics, customers, or features — only use documented proof points, or flag gaps.
- Do not disclose anything marked internal-only (e.g. discounting).
- If a reference file is still a placeholder or missing info the task needs, say so and ask,
  rather than guessing.
- When output would improve or contradict the reference files, suggest an update to keep them current.
